Put the installed cymem, preshed, murmurhash, blis and numpy packages on
Cython's include_path so thinc's cross-package cimports resolve in the
cross-build.

thinc's six Cython modules cimport across package boundaries —
`from cymem.cymem cimport Pool`, `from preshed.maps cimport PreshMap`,
`from murmurhash.mrmr cimport hash64`, `cimport blis.cy` and `cimport numpy
as np` — and every one of those `.pxd` files ships inside the corresponding
installed package. Upstream's setup.py passes Cython only
`numpy.get_include()` and `get_path("include")`, both of which are C header
directories, and leaves the sibling packages to be discovered some other way.
Under forge that discovery fails: crossenv rewrites sysconfig so
`get_path()`/`get_paths()` answer with TARGET paths rather than the build
environment's site-packages, where the build-time dependencies actually live,
and cythonize cannot resolve the cimports when the wheel is built with
`python -m build --no-isolation`. The build stops inside cythonize, before
any compiler runs.

The hunk adds a `_pkg_root()` helper and feeds its results to
`cythonize(..., include_path=...)`:

  * it asks the import system first — `importlib.util.find_spec(pkg)`, then
    the *parent* of each `submodule_search_locations` entry, which is the
    directory Cython wants, because it resolves `preshed.maps` as
    `<dir>/preshed/maps.pxd`;
  * unlike preshed's version of this patch it only checks that the package
    *directory* is there, since the five packages expose different `.pxd`
    names;
  * it falls back to a plain scan of `sys.path`, de-duplicates, and drops
    anything it cannot locate, so the patch can only ever add include
    directories — it cannot turn a working resolution into a hard failure;
  * it imports `os` locally as `_os` because thinc's setup.py uses `pathlib`
    and never imports `os` at module level.

The rationale is recorded in this recipe's meta.yaml comment and in PR #72,
which introduced the whole spacy chain: "Both cythonize without putting the
build env's site-packages on Cython's `include_path`, so their `cimport`s of
cymem/preshed/murmurhash/thinc/numpy can't be resolved in the cross-build …
The patches locate each installed package via the import system and add it to
`include_path` — the same fix preshed already carries." The exact Cython
error text was not captured anywhere, so the failure is described here as
those sources describe it.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
